    formula: null,
    key: "terrain.desert.canyon.transform.position",
    line: null,
    note: "Local to the LevelArt prefab root. WARNING: this used to add \"which the environment scene instantiates at the origin with no overrides (checked)\", and that is FALSE for kauai. `LevelArt_Kauai` is an UNPACKED copy sitting at (-2218, 0, -1691) under `levelOffset`, so kauai placed as `worldOffset + this` lands 2,218 m / 1,691 m from where 2016 has it. Measured through the flattener, which composes the whole chain: kauai terrain world (-4266, 68, -3739) against this local (0, 68, 0), and kauai water world (-19215, -46.08, -17431) against local (-14949, -46.08, -13692) - the SAME (-4266, 0, -3739) on both, of which (-2048, 0, -2048) is levelOffset and the remaining (-2218, 0, -1691) is the env root nothing records. alpine and desert really are zero here, which is why \"(checked)\" survived: it was checked where the wrong answer and the right one agree. DO NOT load a second environment on this field alone until the env root is extracted - see docs/NEXT.md.",
